// MARKETING — Nova's answers AND the Marketing chapter of the studio's
// Documentation page, which is composed from these entries in FILE ORDER: a
// topic's label is the chapter section, its first `about` is the section's
// opening paragraph (rendered without a heading), and every other entry is a
// sub-heading. So within each topic the order is fixed: the introduction, other
// `about` entries, `fields`, `howto`, `settings`, then `troubleshoot`. Nothing
// else is written about Marketing for users — this file is the single source.
//
// MOVED OUT OF `./sales.ts`, 27/09/2026, when the department became a chapter.
// Every entry id it carried there is kept here unchanged; entries elsewhere
// (crmSales.ts, finance.ts) still link to them by id.
//
// DRAWN FROM THE CODE, not from the docs. Where docs/functionality/ and the
// screens disagree, the screens win. Five sentences were corrected against the
// code rather than copied: a Draft campaign may go straight to Running and a
// Paused one straight to Completed (CAMPAIGN_MOVES in modules/marketing/
// model.ts); an event needs a start as well as a name (eventsService.ts);
// events ARE drawn on the calendar, which events.md listed as not built until
// 27/09/2026 (StudioMarketingCalendar.js, planning.ts); a form is opened and
// closed with buttons, not a "who can answer" select, and its name, company,
// phone and email mapping appears only once it has a rule (StudioFormEditor.js,
// Settings); and the partner form asks the owner and whether the arrangement
// is running BEFORE what was agreed (StudioMarketingPartners.js).
//
// THREE BOUNDARIES THE ANSWERS HOLD. Leads stay Sales tickets: Marketing sends
// and reads them, and never assigns or works them (leads.md). Marketing-budget
// owns NO collection: a cost is a Finance bill or expense carrying a campaign,
// read where Finance files it (marketing-budget.md). And the consent ledger is
// APPEND-ONLY, its addresses sealed at rest (audiences.md). nompany records
// marketing work and sends nothing.
//
// Every `fields` entry names, in a comment above it, the component and schema
// (src/modules/marketing/schema.ts) its list was checked against. What a doc
// lists under "Not built yet" is answered here as NOT AVAILABLE YET, never as a
// feature. ENTRY IDS ARE FOREVER: rewrite the words freely; never rename an id.
